  {
    "sha": "2acc52c3e2d831b2be32e414c078393c713f90be",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVyT_AdoAKDJhY2M1MmMzZTJkODMxYjJiZTMyZTQxNGMwNzgzOTNjNzEzZjkwYmU",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-27T22:17:58Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-27T22:17:58Z"
      },
      "message": "test(post): record LinuxCNC full-diameter drilling on a machine\n\nThe machine-less LinuxCNC case refuses on the missing safe retract\nalone, so it did not check the drilling depth. The case now also posts\non vmc.mch (a stated safe retract) and records the NC golden\ndrill_full_diameter_on_machine.nc with G73 ... Z-12.803.\n\nA guard in recorded_streams checks each post golden dir: a post with a\nmill drilling cycle has an NC golden of drill_full_diameter (plain or\n_on_machine) with the depth 12.803. Posts with no such cycle are an\nexplicit list. Heidenhain Klartext is a named gap: it refuses a tool\nwith no stated kind, and the recorded stream states none.\n\nPinned by script_linuxcnc::drill_full_diameter_on_a_machine_posts_the_full_diameter_depth\nand recorded_streams::each_drilling_post_records_the_full_diameter_depth.\n\nRefs #2528\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
